#!/usr/bin/env python3
# nctop: a read-only terminal dashboard for a NanoClaw v2 install.
#
#   tools/nctop/nctop                       the dashboard (press ? for keys)
#   tools/nctop/nctop --dump VIEW [ARG]     print one view as text and exit (overview|sessions|tasks|logs|paths|
#                                           files [dir]|file <path>|session <id> [--messages] [--verbose])
#
# Tabs: Overview (service, host, agents, running sessions, what needs attention, next tasks, containers), Sessions
# (Enter follows one: the agent's own transcript with tool calls, or the inbound/outbound messages), Tasks, Logs (the
# host log, followed), Files (the agent folders: CLAUDE.md, skills, memory, task logs).
#
# Read-only by construction: the central data comes from `ncl <resource> list --json`; the per-session mailboxes
# (data/v2-sessions/<group>/<session>/{inbound,outbound}.db, which ncl has no resource for) are opened with mode=ro;
# the only other commands are the service manager's status (systemctl --user show, or launchctl list) and docker
# ps/stats. Nothing writes. Python 3 standard library only.
#
# Run it as the user the install belongs to (on a dedicated service account: sudo -u <account> tools/nctop/nctop):
# transcripts are private to that user. NANOCLAW_DIR overrides the install root (default: two levels above this file).

